    {
      "id": "M2130-P0-01",
      "severity": "P0",
      "title": "The ICC2 SPEF producer cannot satisfy the literal routed.spef admission gate",
      "evidence": "M2129 Tcl invokes write_parasitics with -output $axis_dir/output/routed.spef. Installed ICC2 V-2023.12-SP3 documentation states that -output is a prefix and the emitted SPEF name is <file_name>.<parasitic_tech_name>_<temperature>[...].spef, plus a .spef_scenario file. The one-shot runner then requires the literal nonsymlink output/routed.spef. Therefore a real ICC2 run produces a suffixed file such as routed.spef.<corner>.spef and deterministically fails the runner's literal-name check after consuming the unique attempt.",
      "minimum_fix": "Under a fresh source identity, emit to a dedicated raw prefix, require exactly one regular nonsymlink corner SPEF from the requested tt_power corner, validate that it is not the scenario map, and atomically canonicalize that raw SPEF to output/routed.spef before the existing strict parser runs. Keep the parser strict; do not widen it to glob or accept .spef_scenario.",
      "m2131_effect": "PROHIBITED"
    }
